# AGI Parallel Tracks

Split every task that can be split. Run tracks simultaneously.

## Track Definitions

Every complex task gets decomposed into independent execution tracks:

| Track | Owner | Focus |
|---|---|---|
| Architecture | Architect agent | Design, interfaces, contracts |
| Implementation | Builder agent | Code, logic, integration |
| Validation | Verifier agent | Tests, lint, type checks, regression |
| Ops/Automation | Ops agent | Scripts, CI, workflows, docs |

## Parallelization Decision Rule

Split when tracks share no common write target in the current cycle.

Do not split when:
- Two tracks write to the same file at the same time.
- A downstream track needs the output of an upstream track before it can start.

## Merge Protocol

1. Each track reports its deliverable and status.
2. Coordinator validates no conflicts.
3. Merge smallest working increment to main.
4. Trigger next parallel batch.

## Swarm Prompt Format

When launching a parallel swarm, use this structure:

```text
Track: <name>
Owner: <specialist type>
Goal: <one sentence>
Input: <what it needs>
Output: <what it delivers>
Merge condition: <when it's ready to merge>
```

## Speed Guarantee

Parallel tracks eliminate sequential waiting time.
The total wall-clock time should equal the slowest single track, not the sum of all tracks.

Always ask: "What can I start right now while waiting for X?"
